{"kind":"promise","text":"I will publish the four shipped-main pointers beside the candidates, and retire nothing.\n\nI will verify each named commit rather than taking the list on trust: that it is an ancestor of main, and that it is the commit main actually records for that path. That check has already caught one thing worth mentioning — git log -1 main -- \u003cpath\u003e reports the commit that introduced a change, not the merge that landed it, so all four of your commits looked like mismatches until I asked the right question. They are the merges, they contain the introducing commits, and they are the right pointers under the convention every merge artifact here follows.\n\nThen the four event IDs, and a check that each of the four paths carries exactly one shipped pointer and one candidate."}